course: dictionary
lesson: 7913
title: One word, different meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the words around it, which is its context. «Don't be so ratty» means grumpy in British talk, because the speaker is telling someone to stop being cross. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The same word can mean something quite different in another country. In the US, «ratty» describes clothes that are old, torn and shabby, like a «ratty old jumper». Context tells you which meaning is meant: a grumpy person, or a worn-out jumper.
explain: A capital letter is a clue too. «Ratty» with a capital R is a name, like the friendly Water Rat in The Wind in the Willows. Ratty is Mole's best friend, and he loves «messing about in boats». He is not really a rat: he is a water vole.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Ratty» (UK, Australia, New Zealand, informal) means bad-tempered and easily annoyed; grumpy.
fact: «Ratty» (US, informal) means shabby, old and torn.
fact: «Ratty» can also mean like a rat, or full of rats.
fact: Ratty, with a capital R, is the friendly name of the Water Rat in The Wind in the Willows.
exercise: «Don't be so ratty.» What does ratty mean here? | Full of rats | *Grumpy and easily annoyed | Torn and shabby | A friendly river animal
exercise: In the US, a «ratty old jumper» is one that is what? | Brand new and bright | Full of rats | *Old, shabby and torn | Very warm and thick
exercise: Who is Ratty in The Wind in the Willows? | A rat who lives in a sewer | Toad's grumpy cousin | A badger who lives in a wood | *Mole's best friend, the Water Rat
test: In «Thank you so much, dear Ratty!», what kind of word is Ratty? | *A name, with a capital R | A kind of boat | A rat in a sewer | A describing word
test: Which sentence uses ratty to mean grumpy? | *«Stop being so ratty, you are upsetting everyone.» | «The ratty old boat sank in the river.» | «The ratty jumper had holes in both sleeves.» | «Ratty» was swimming in the river.
exam: In «Don't be so ratty», ratty means grumpy, not shabby, because | *The sentence is about how a person is feeling and behaving | The sentence describes an old boat | The sentence is about clothes | The sentence names a river animal
